Adam initially has 48 books. After selling 19 books, he has:

$$
48 - 19 = 29 \text{ books remaining}.
$$

He then uses the money from the sale to buy 38 new books. Adding these to the remaining books:

$$
29 + 38 = 67 \text{ books}.
$$

