The total number of books to be put away is 46. The librarian takes 10 books, leaving Oliver with $46 - 10 = 36$ books. If Oliver can fit 4 books on each shelf, the number of shelves needed is calculated by dividing the remaining books by the number of books per shelf:

$$
\frac{36}{4} = 9
$$

Thus, Oliver will need $\boxed{9}$ shelves.

